{"Title":"An Act authorizing certain public employees’ creditable retirement service","BillNumber":"H2619","DocketNumber":"HD1026","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"JJO1","Name":"James J. O'Day","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JJO1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T01:21:30.66"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"JJO1","Name":"James J. O'Day","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JJO1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T01:21:30.66"},{"Id":"DMD1","Name":"Daniel M. Donahue","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/DMD1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-02T12:51:53.59"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H2619/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative O'Day of West Boylston, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 2619) of James J. O'Day and Daniel M. Donahue relative to authorizing certain public employees’ creditable retirement service.  Public Service.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 4 of Chapter 32 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 378, the words “Peace Corps” and inserting in the place thereof the words:- Peace Corps, Vista or AmeriCorps\r\n\tSECTION 2. Section 4 of Chapter 32 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting, in line 380, after the words “guidance counselor” the following words:- state employee\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J23","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J23"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}